# Data and contracts

## MikroORM

- Entities stay next to their feature module. A schema change is: edit the entity, then `pnpm --filter @sokil/api mikro-orm migration:create`, then review the SQL in `apps/api/src/migrations/`.
- Migrations are forward-only. Deploy runs `mikro-orm migration:up` before the API process. Do not hand-edit an already shipped migration; add a new one.
- Relations use MikroORM collections. A loose string id is a bug unless the master plan explicitly keeps one (training `equipmentSetId` is an existing loose id).
- Hide secrets on the entity (`hidden: true`): password hashes, reset tokens, session hashes.
- Seeders must keep the `NODE_ENV === 'production'` early return. No new well-known passwords.

## Shared types

- Values used by both apps (roles, notification types, achievement ids, stable response DTOs) go in `packages/shared-types` and are imported from the package, not copied.
- Request bodies that need runtime validation stay as class-validator classes in `apps/api/**/dto`. Do not validate HTTP bodies with Zod. Zod is for API env (`env.zod.ts`).
- Web-only view state stays in the web app. Do not put React types in `shared-types`.
- After changing the package, consumers import the built export. Root `pnpm dev` / `pnpm lint` build it first; a filtered command may not.

## Client API types

- `apps/web/src/services/types.ts` re-exports shared types. Add a new cross-app field to `shared-types` instead of a parallel interface.
- Domain HTTP helpers share one client that sets `credentials: 'include'`, `Accept-Language`, timeout, and `X-CSRF-Token` on POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE.
